virglrenderer: core profile shaders ask for GLSL 3.30, no extensions that are core

What: on a desktop core profile that supports GLSL 3.30 (macOS: 4.10), every
translated shader is "#version 330" or newer instead of 140/150. "#extension"
lines are left out when the emitted version has the feature in core, from one
table (ext_core_glsl_ver, used by every desktop "#extension" in emit_header):
ARB_texture_rectangle, ARB_draw_instanced and ARB_uniform_buffer_object (1.40),
ARB_texture_multisample and ARB_fragment_coord_conventions (1.50),
ARB_shader_bit_encoding and ARB_explicit_attrib_location (3.30), and the 4.00/
4.10 ones for shaders that need those versions. ARB_texture_query_lod is not in
the table: the translation writes its textureQueryLOD() spelling.
Why: Apple's core profile refuses floatBitsToInt()/intBitsToFloat() and friends
below 3.30, and many translations use them without setting SHADER_REQ_INTS (e.g.
integer vertex attributes passed on: dEQP-GLES3.functional.shaders.precision.int.*).
It also refuses "#extension GL_ARB_draw_instanced" (Chrome's instanced WebGL
shaders). One refused shader stopped the guest's whole GL context, so every
later draw of that app was black (dEQP-GLES3 in one process: 455/896 pass).
Upstreamable (desktop core profiles only; GLES and compatibility hosts are
unchanged); not sent.
Overlap: gpu-robust's virgl-core-instance-id.patch does the ARB_draw_instanced
part only. This patch leaves the upstream ARB_texture_rectangle line in place
and adds its check above it, so both patches apply in either order (checked);
drop virgl-core-instance-id.patch when both land.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c (generated GLSL compiled by the
Mac's OpenGL; every case checks the version and extension lines; fails without
this patch).
